The generated prompt names the output `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Charging/**`.
That directory is NOT a compiled source root: project.yml registers ONLY
`Sources`, `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets`, `TeslaSync/feature-views`, `Localization`,
and the generated DesignTokens for both app targets; `.swiftlint.yml` `included:`
matches the same set. All 1436 existing P4 surfaces live in `TeslaSync/feature-views`.
Placing the page anywhere else would (a) NOT compile into the app, (b) NOT be linted,
and (c) require editing project.yml (predecessor bypass, covenant #7). The page is
therefore shipped in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/ChargingHeatmapPage.*` — the
real, build-verifiable home — following the ChargingDetailSection (0053) decomposition
exactly. The placeholder-gate `-Path` is the real feature-views tree accordingly.

